redis consumer producer
redis_conn = redis.StrictRedis(host='localhost', port=6379, password='', decode_responses=True)
### Producer (push)
```python
qs = ["abc"]
redis_conn.lpush("my_queue", json.dumps(qs))
```

### Consumer (pop)
```python
raw = redis_conn.rpop("my_queue")
if raw:
    data = json.loads(raw)

# my_queue not existed, would return None immediatly, not waiting
```
redis can do api cache, distribute lock, producer/consumer, shared variable in multiple instance

